{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'pwd; ls -la; cat VENUE.md; for f in .codex/skills/{write-paper-standalone,validate-paper,memory-log,scientific-evidence,generate-concept-figure}/SKILL.md; do echo \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"/workspace/paper\ntotal 10956\ndrwx------ 6 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 04:18 .\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 04:02 ..\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     747 Nov  7 04:02 .agentic_paper_workspace.json\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 04:03 .codex\nprw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov  7 04:18 .paper_stream_20261107_040258.fifo\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov  7 04:02 .paper_two_stage_enabled\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    3685 Nov  7 04:18 VENUE.md\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 04:02 figures\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent      16 Nov  7 04:02 global_memory -> ../investigation\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   13786 Nov  7 04:03 global_memory_recent.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    6020 Nov  7 04:03 global_memory_summary.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    8748 Nov  7 04:18 memory.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   26973 Nov  2 14:28 paper.bst\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    8934 Nov  2 14:28 paper.sty\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov  7 04:18 paper_agent_codex_20261107_040258.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 9047640 Nov  7 04:03 paper_data.json\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 04:08 paper_diagnostics\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov  7 04:02 paper_diagnostics_20261107_040258_42062.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    4936 Nov  7 04:18 paper_events_20261107_040258.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     791 Nov  7 04:02 paper_prep_20261107_040258.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   72461 Nov  7 04:18 paper_prompt.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   29013 Nov  7 04:17 paper_strategy.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   20934 Nov  7 04:17 paper_strategy.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  490736 Nov  7 04:18 paper_strategy_agent_codex_20261107_040258.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   46258 Nov  7 04:10 paper_strategy_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     331 Nov  7 04:18 paper_strategy_resolution.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    8111 Nov  7 04:08 reference_query_plan.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    8721 Nov  7 04:08 reference_query_plan.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 1257671 Nov  7 04:08 reference_query_plan_agent_codex_20261107_040258.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   30267 Nov  7 04:03 reference_query_plan_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     265 Nov  7 04:08 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     279 Nov  7 04:08 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    3245 Nov  7 04:10 reference_retrieval.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    7699 Nov  7 04:10 references.bib\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   26441 Nov  7 04:10 references_provenance.json\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent      16 Nov  7 04:02 results -> ../investigation\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 04:03 source_evidence\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     265 Nov  7 04:18 strategy_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     271 Nov  7 04:18 strategy_validation_feedback.md\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent       7 Nov  7 04:02 task -> ../task\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\n.codex/skills/{write-paper-standalone,validate-paper,memory-log,scientific-evidence,generate-concept-figure}/SKILL.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
