{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat .codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md; cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; sed -n '1,100p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py; rg -n 'apply_patch|codex.*internal' memory.md; ls /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex* -d 2>/dev/null; readlink -f \"'$(command -v codex); ls task/resources/final; python - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json')); e=p['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes'];\nfor ep in e:\n print('seed',ep['seed'],'replay',ep['solution']['replay'])\n for c in ep['solution']['cases']:\n  if c['case']=='original':\n   print(c['family']);\n   for o in c['observations']:print(o['target'],o['rule'],o['fraction'],o['allocation']['status'],len(o['allocation']['tasks']),o['reference']['lower'],o['reference']['upper'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat .codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md; cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; sed -n '1,100p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py; rg -n 'apply_patch|codex.*internal' memory.md; ls /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex* -d 2>/dev/null; readlink -f \"'$(command -v codex); ls task/resources/final; python - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json')); e=p['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes'];\nfor ep in e:\n print('seed',ep['seed'],'replay',ep['solution']['replay'])\n for c in ep['solution']['cases']:\n  if c['case']=='original':\n   print(c['family']);\n   for o in c['observations']:print(o['target'],o['rule'],o['fraction'],o['allocation']['status'],len(o['allocation']['tasks']),o['reference']['lower'],o['reference']['upper'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: retrieve-references\ndescription: Retrieve grounded BibTeX references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (`scholarly`) and write references.bib plus provenance JSON for paper generation.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nFetch references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (via `scholarly`) and keep only real BibTeX entries.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final report/paper generation.\n- Related-work section needs grounded citations.\n\n# What to do\n1. Build focused search queries from task goal, method names, and top experiment ideas.\n2. Preferred path (Semantic Scholar Graph API):\n```bash\npython scripts/s2_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n3. Fallback path (OpenAlex):\n```bash\npython scripts/openalex_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 10 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Optional:\n   - `--mailto you@example.com` to enter the OpenAlex polite pool\n   - Env fallback: `OPENALEX_EMAIL`\n4. Alternate path (Google Scholar API wrapper with `scholarly`):\n```bash\npython -m pip install scholarly\npython scripts/scholarly_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 25 \\\n  --sort-by relevance \\\n  --proxy-mode auto \\\n  --delay-seconds 0.5 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Proxy options:\n   - `--proxy-mode auto|none|free|single`\n   - `--proxy-http <url>` / `--proxy-https <url>` for `single`\n   - Env fallbacks: `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_MODE`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTP`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTPS`\n   - Global `HTTP_PROXY` / `HTTPS_PROXY` are intentionally ignored to avoid accidental ambient proxying\n5. Require `S2_API_KEY` when available for `s2_fetch.py` (script reads env automatically).\n6. Keep only references with valid BibTeX and citation key.\n7. Dedupe by citation key and paper id.\n8. Fail hard if references found `< min-refs`.\n9. Use `s2_fetch.py` first for stability, `openalex_fetch.py` as the next fallback, and `scholarly_fetch.py` last if the other sources fail.\n\n# Outputs\n- `references.bib`\n- `references_provenance.json`\n\n# Notes\n- Use `templates/provenance.schema.json` for expected shape.\n{\n  \"$id\": \"https://schemas.agentic-scientist.local/scientific-evidence/artifact-manifest.schema.json\",\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"artifact\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"source\",\n            \"derived\",\n            \"manuscript\",\n            \"figure\",\n            \"table\",\n            \"script\",\n            \"log\",\n            \"other\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"media_type\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"description\": \"Path to the artifact relative to the scientific-evidence root when possible.\",\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"sha256\": {\n          \"description\": \"Optional hash recorded when the producing workflow computes one.\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"path\",\n        \"kind\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"derived_from\": {\n      \"description\": \"Inline @evidence refs or stable ids describing the artifact inputs.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"minLength\": 1,\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"generated_by\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"command\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"minLength\": 1,\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"cwd\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"finished_at\": {\n          \"format\": \"date-time\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"script_path\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"script_sha256\": {\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"started_at\": {\n          \"format\": \"date-time\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"script_path\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"named_outputs\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": [\n          \"string\",\n          \"number\",\n          \"integer\",\n          \"boolean\",\n          \"array\",\n          \"object\",\n          \"null\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Optional machine-readable outputs emitted by the derivation.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"notes\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"schema_name\": {\n      \"const\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"schema_name\",\n    \"artifact\",\n    \"derived_from\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Scientific Evidence Artifact Manifest\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\"\"\"Deterministic counterfactual allocation solver; no training or external files.\n\nProtocol: handle(dict) -> finite JSON dict. Extra request/response keys are forbidden.\nEvery episode starts with reset, clearing all arrays, transfer buffers and RNG.\nSeeds are arbitrary nonnegative integers and initialize RNG only, not workloads.\n\nreset: {op:'reset', seed:int} -> {ok:true}.\nupload_start: {op, encoding:'base64', dtype:'<f8', shape:[models,tasks],\n byte_length:int, chunk_count:int, sha256:64-char hex, task_ids:[str,...]}\n -> {ok:true}. Models 2..100000, tasks 2..100, bytes exactly models*tasks*8,\n logical limit 16 MiB; chunk_count=ceil(bytes/1048576), in 1..16.\nupload_chunk: {op, index:int, data:base64 str} -> {ok:true}; contiguous zero-based\n indices, each decoded block <=1048576 bytes, all except last full-sized.\nupload_commit: {op} -> {ok:true}; checks digest, finite [0,1] scores and shape.\n All buffering is candidate-owned memory; no host filenames or shared files.\nsolve: {op, targets:[distinct row int,...], rules:['mean','median','borda'],\n cap_fractions:[float,float], tolerance:1e-10, work_seconds:positive float}\n -> {solutions:[{status:str,tasks:[distinct column int,...]},...]}. At most\n eight targets; decisions are target-major, then rule-major, then cap-major.\n A selected coordinate is set to score + fraction*(1-score), fraction in [0,1].\n Both fractions can be zero for no-update experiments. Costs are one per\n selected coordinate, divided by task count for reported investment.\n Input scores/caps round to 10 decimal places before evaluation. Mean and\n median use float64; Borda is average pairwise win credit (ties half), updated\n competitors included. Co-first allows an aggregate deficit <= tolerance.\n status is 'feasible' (tasks witness), 'unattainable' (tasks=[]; full caps\n cannot win), or 'unresolved' (tasks=[]; honest bounded solver uncertainty).\n No optimality or internal-state self-report is accepted. Evaluator independently\n checks witnesses, ranks, unattainability and controls; no answers are returned.\n After one solve, release {op:'release'} -> {ok:true} clears episode buffers.\n No additional response fields, logs on stdout, file paths, polling, retries,\n state transfers, candidate-chosen objectives or hidden telemetry are supported.\n Maximum response: 48 decisions with at most 100 integer indices each, <64 KiB.\n reset -> upload_start -> upload_chunk(s) -> upload_commit -> solve -> release.\n A method may replace the solver below while preserving this exact interface.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport itertools\nimport math\nimport random\nimport time\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n_state = {}\n\n\ndef _rank_totals(matrix):\n    result = np.zeros(matrix.shape[0], dtype=np.int64)\n    for column in matrix.T:\n        _, inverse, counts = np.unique(column, return_inverse=True, return_counts=True)\n        below = np.cumsum(counts) - counts\n        result += 2 * below[inverse] + counts[inverse] - 1\n    return result\n\n\ndef _answer(indices):\n    return {'status': 'feasible', 'tasks': sorted(int(column) for column in indices)}\n\n\ndef _exhaustive(original, caps, wins):\n    available = np.flatnonzero(caps > original).tolist()\n    for size in range(len(available) + 1):\n        for subset in itertools.combinations(available, size):\n            indices = list(subset)\n            if wins(indices):\n                return indices\n    return None\n\n\ndef _mean_budget(original, caps, wins):\n    order = np.argsort(-(caps - original), kind='stable')\n    for size in range(len(order) + 1):\n        selected = order[:size].tolist()\n        if wins(selected):\n            return selected\n    return None\n\n\ndef _odd_median_budget(original, caps, competitor, tolerance):\n    already_above = np.count_nonzero(original - competitor >= -tolerance)\n    promotable = np.flatnonzero(\n        (original - competitor < -tolerance) & (caps - competitor >= -tolerance)\n    )\n    needed = max(0, len(original) // 2 + 1 - already_above)\n    if needed > len(promotable):\n        return None\n    return promotable[:needed].tolist()\n\n\ndef _even_median_budget(original, caps, competitor, tolerance, wins):\n    half = len(original) // 2\n    endpoints = np.unique(np.concatenate((original, caps)))\n    best = None\n    for lower in endpoints:\n        upper_candidates = endpoints[\n            (endpoints >= lower)\n            & ((endpoints + lower) / 2 - competitor >= -tolerance)\n19:- summary: Correction: the preceding final-status event was premature; output creation failed because apply_patch was not on PATH, so schema validation did not run. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Tooling failure changes no scientific conclusion.\n20:- evidence: Shell reported apply_patch: not found, followed by FileNotFoundError for reference_query_plan.json; no plan files were created by that attempt.\n24:- summary: reference_query_plan_ready confirmed: both files now exist and schema/mirroring validation passed. Used the installed Codex internal apply_patch dispatcher after the PATH utility was unavailable. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Reference planning scopes observations without revising scientific recommendations.\n/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex\n/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/bin/codex.js\nhelm.json\nopenllm.json\nprotocol.json\nseed 42011 replay {'correct': True, 'duration_seconds': 2.053458292968571, 'failure': None, 'signature': [['feasible', 1], ['feasible', 1], ['feasible', 0], ['feasible', 0], ['feasible', 4], ['feasible', 4], ['feasible', 9], ['feasible', 23], ['feasible', 12], ['feasible', 12], ['feasible', 34], ['feasible', 39], ['feasible', 12], ['feasible', 36], ['feasible', 16], ['feasible', 16], ['feasible', 41], ['feasible', 50], ['feasible', 13], ['feasible', 40], ['feasible', 18], ['feasible', 18], ['feasible', 41], ['feasible', 52], ['feasible', 16], ['feasible', 49], ['feasible', 21], ['feasible', 21], ['feasible', 46], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 21], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 24], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 50], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 25], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 29], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 51], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 46], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 29], ['unattainable', 0], ['feasible', 53], ['unattainable', 0]]}\nhelm\n40 mean 1.0 feasible 1 1 1\n40 mean 0.5 feasible 1 1 1\n40 median 1.0 feasible 0 0 0\n40 median 0.5 feasible 0 0 0\n40 borda 1.0 feasible 4 4 4\n40 borda 0.5 feasible 4 4 4\n10 mean 1.0 feasible 9 9 9\n10 mean 0.5 feasible 23 23 23\n10 median 1.0 feasible 12 12 12\n10 median 0.5 feasible 12 12 12\n10 borda 1.0 feasible 34 34 34\n10 borda 0.5 feasible 39 39 39\n37 mean 1.0 feasible 12 12 12\n37 mean 0.5 feasible 36 36 36\n37 median 1.0 feasible 16 16 16\n37 median 0.5 feasible 16 16 16\n37 borda 1.0 feasible 41 41 41\n37 borda 0.5 feasible 50 50 50\n18 mean 1.0 feasible 13 13 13\n18 mean 0.5 feasible 40 40 40\n18 median 1.0 feasible 18 18 18\n18 median 0.5 feasible 18 18 18\n18 borda 1.0 feasible 41 41 41\n18 borda 0.5 feasible 52 52 52\n28 mean 1.0 feasible 16 16 16\n28 mean 0.5 feasible 49 49 49\n28 median 1.0 feasible 21 21 21\n28 median 0.5 feasible 21 21 21\n28 borda 1.0 feasible 46 46 4