g individual-rival bounds and suffix pruning. Search is bounded by a deadline and a node limit; on interruption it returns a verified incumbent, not an optimality assertion. In the recorded original instances, independent reference bounds close and match every finite returned cardinality. That observed agreement is stronger than a feasible-witness check, but it does not establish exactness for arbitrary larger instances or superiority of a particular search component. No controlled component ablation is available.\n+The supplied selected source builds a feasible gain-ordered prefix, deletes unnecessary tasks, and searches smaller cardinalities using individual-rival bounds and suffix pruning. Search is bounded by a deadline and a node limit; on interruption it returns a verified incumbent, not an optimality assertion. In the recorded original instances, independent reference bounds close and match every finite returned cardinality. That observed agreement is stronger than a feasible-witness check, but it does not establish exactness for arbitrary larger instances or superiority of a particular search component. No controlled component ablation is available.\n@@\n-\\\\caption{Paired minimum task fractions for identical targets. Top: HELM; bottom: Open LLM. Left: full headroom; right: half headroom. NA rails indicate certified unattainability, not missing values or an additional numeric range. Annotated targets reverse their mean--median ordering. Labels \"'$'\"\\\\times k\"'$ denote coincident target points. All finite points have matching independent lower and upper cardinality bounds.}\n+'\"\\\\caption{Paired minimum task fractions for identical targets. Top: HELM; bottom: Open LLM. Left: full headroom; right: half headroom. NA rails indicate certified unattainability, not missing values or an additional numeric range. Annotated row indices identify targets that reverse their mean--median ordering. Labels \"'$'\"\\\\times k\"'$ denote coincident target points. All 