l finite points have matching independent lower and upper cardinality bounds.}\n@@\n-The selected entry point is specified in\n+The supplied selected entry point is specified in\n@@\n-% @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py]]\n+The retained entry-point file is byte-identical to the downstream selected source. The final manifest records a separate tree digest; different digest scopes are not equated to a file-identity proof. Detailed settings above describe the inspectable selected source, while numerical conclusions rest on the independent recorded allocations and bounds. The retained evaluator source is byte-identical to the evaluator digest in the final manifest.\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py]]\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n)\"; { printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '*** Begin Patch' '*** Add File: source_evidence/evaluation.py'; sed 's/\"'^/+/'\"' task/evaluate_final.py; printf '%s\\\\n' '*** End Patch'; } | (codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \\\"\"'$(cat)\"); /agent-tmp/paper-tools/bin/python scripts/stage_resources.py > /agent-tmp/stage.log; /agent-tmp/paper-tools/bin/python scripts/build_results.py > /agent-tmp/results.log; /agent-tmp/paper-tools/bin/python scripts/reproduce_allocations.py; /agent-tmp/paper-tools/bin/python .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .'","aggregated_output":"Verified recorded witnesses and cap infeasibility: 288\nClaims validation failed: scientific-evidence verifier found 1 dangling `@evidence[[...]]` link(s). scripts/stage_resources.py @evidence[[\" + url + \"]] -> Target did not resolve to a file path, URI, or known ledger id. Fix or remove every dangling link, rerun `scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir <paper_dir>`, and repeat until zero dangling references remain.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
