{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_165","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$(cat <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-At full headroom, all eight targets in each table are reachable under all three rules. At half headroom, HELM has five reachable targets under mean, five under median, and four under Borda; Open LLM has seven, six, and three. Figure~\\\\ref{fig:reachability} uses the same target denominator throughout. An all-task cap that fails the rank condition certifies these unattainable cases. Such a result is a limit of the intervention model, not evidence of an unsuccessful training run or a solver timeout.\n+At full headroom, all eight targets in each table are reachable under all three rules. This is expected structurally: selecting every coordinate sets the target to the scale maximum. The informative full-headroom quantity is therefore the minimum task budget, not reachability alone. At half headroom, HELM has five reachable targets under mean, five under median, and four under Borda; Open LLM has seven, six, and three. Figure~\\\\ref{fig:reachability} uses the same target denominator throughout. An all-task cap that fails the rank condition certifies these unattainable cases. Such a result is a limit of the intervention model, not evidence of an unsuccessful training run or a solver timeout.\n*** Update File: scripts/build_claims.py\n@@\n     add(\\\"There are eight fixed mean-nonwinner rank-spaced targets per score table; three seeds 42011,42013,42017 repeat the same instances; 48 decisions per family, 96 distinct original instances, 288 original records.\\\",\n         artifacts=[\\\"derived/summary.json\\\", \\\"data/protocol.json\\\"])\n+    add(\\\"Within any fixed rule and target, increasing rho weakly decreases the minimum budget, including infinity; this does not order different rules. Full-headroom all-task reachability follows structurally from the intervention model.\\\",\n+        artifacts=[\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py:260\\\", \\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py:193\\\"])\n@@\n-    add(\\\"Mean sorted gains, odd-median threshold counting, even-median endpoint counting and rival-aware Borda integer gap constraints describe the inspected evaluated implementation; Borda search has 20000-node limit, 0.9 work allowance and verified incumbent fallback. Exhaustive scalar verification is used when d<=6.\\\",\n+    add(\\\"Mean sorted gains, odd-median threshold counting, even-median endpoint counting and rival-aware Borda integer gap constraints describe the inspectable supplied selected source; its tree-digest scope is not equated to the final manifest. Borda search has 20000-node limit, 0.9 work allowance and verified incumbent fallback. Exhaustive scalar verification is used when d<=6.\\\",\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n)\\\"; /agent-tmp/paper-tools/bin/python scripts/build_claims.py; PATH=/agent-tmp/paper-bin:/agent-tmp/paper-tools/bin:\"'$PATH bash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex > /agent-tmp/latex.log 2>&1; /agent-tmp/paper-tools/bin/python - <<'\"'PY'\nimport pymupdf\np=pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\nfor index in [5,6,7]:p[index].get_pixmap(matrix=pymupdf.Matrix(1.5,1.5)).save('/agent-tmp/paper-page'+str(index+1)+'.png')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
